{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.1-structure", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1 (structure)"}, "paraphrase": "Atharvan tells Śāṇḍilya: there are eight limbs — ten yamas, ten niyamas, eight postures, three prāṇāyāmas, five pratyāhāras, dhāraṇā, two kinds of dhyāna and one samādhi.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:sandilya-eight-limbs"], "teachers": ["tch:atharvan", "tch:sandilya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.1-yamas", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1 (yamas)"}, "paraphrase": "Non-injury is causing no pain to any being by mind, speech or body; truth is speaking what is true and beneficial; … purity is external (earth and water) and internal (by knowledge of the Self).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-yamas-ten-niyamas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.15", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.15"}, "paraphrase": "Fourteen principal channels; the suṣumnā is the path to liberation; the moon (tamas, nectar) moves in iḍā, the sun (rajas, poison) in piṅgalā; suṣumnā devours time.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis", "cpt:inner-time"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.16", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.16"}, "paraphrase": "The qualified practitioner lives in a hermitage, worships Vināyaka and his chosen deity, and purifies the channels.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:nadi-sodhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.17", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.17"}, "paraphrase": "Praṇava is prāṇāyāma; a is Gāyatrī (red, on a swan, a girl), u Sāvitrī (white, on Garuḍa, youthful), m Sarasvatī (black, on a bull, aged).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.2", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.2"}, "paraphrase": "Niyamas: worship of the Lord is worshipping Viṣṇu, Rudra and the others with a clear mind; hearing the doctrine is inquiring into Vedānta; japa is loud, whispered (a thousand times better) or mental (a crore times better).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:japa-kinds"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.23", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.23"}, "paraphrase": "As a lion, elephant or tiger is tamed gradually, so breath is to be controlled; otherwise it kills the practitioner.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "obstacles": ["obs:improper-pranayama"], "notes": "Parallel to Haṭhayogapradīpikā 2.15.", "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.31-kevala", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.31 (kevala)"}, "paraphrase": "When kevala-kumbhaka is mastered the kuṇḍalinī awakens and the suṣumnā is freed of obstruction; signs appear. Method not reproduced.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "practices": ["prc:kevala-kumbhaka"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.31-vaisnavi", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.31 (vaiṣṇavī)"}, "paraphrase": "Vaiṣṇavī mudrā: the target within, the gaze outward without blinking — secret in all tantras.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:vaisnavi-mudra", "prc:sambhavi-mudra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.41", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.41"}, "paraphrase": "There are two ways of destroying the mind: yoga, the stopping of its modifications, and knowledge, right seeing; for some yoga is impossible, for others knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:yoga-jnana-samuccaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.42-53", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.42-53"}, "paraphrase": "Ways of stilling the vibration of prāṇa (shared with the Yoga Vāsiṣṭha): study, association with the wise, dispassion, practice, fixing on one object, restraint of breath, meditation on the heart-space, and others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasana-ksaya-manonasa-tattvajnana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.54", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.54"}, "paraphrase": "The kuṇḍalinī rising above the throat gives liberation to yogins; remaining below it binds the ignorant.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.60-68", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.60-68"}, "paraphrase": "Saṃyama on parts and principles gives powers: on the body's parts knowledge of the worlds; on merit and demerit knowledge of past and future; on the throat freedom from hunger; on the kūrma-nāḍī steadiness; on the light in the head vision of siddhas; and others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "practices": ["prc:samyama-yoga-upanisads"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhis-in-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.69", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.69"}, "paraphrase": "Five pratyāhāras: forcibly withdrawing the senses; seeing all as the Self; renouncing the fruits of daily acts; turning from all objects; and holding (the breath) at the eighteen vital points in ascending and descending order.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:five-pratyaharas", "prc:marmasthana-dharana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.70-72", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.70-72"}, "paraphrase": "Dhāraṇā is threefold (fixing mind in the Self, outer space in the heart-space, the five deities in the elements); dhyāna is with qualities (form) or without (the Self's nature); samādhi is the union of jīvātman and paramātman free from the triad.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "ultimate"], "practices": ["prc:saguna-nirguna-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:2", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Śāṇḍilya, not finding brahmavidyā in the four Vedas, asks Atharvan; Brahman is truth, knowledge, infinite, and 'that you are'.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "teacher-transmission"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sandilya-upanisad:3", "source": "src:sandilya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "Brahman has three forms — with parts, without parts, and with-and-without parts; its most manifest form is Dattātreya, who gave himself to Atri and was born of Anasūyā; his meditation form is the naked avadhūta smeared with ash.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:sakala-niskala"], "teachers": ["tch:dattatreya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
